---
const videoId = "zMd6IJ-6e-8";
const videoTitle = "Meet Joe Dampt: Joe's Vintage Guitars";
---

<section class="vdo-sct" id="meet-joe">
  <div class="vdo-sct__inner">
    <!-- Cream backdrop pseudo + rust triangle pseudo handled in CSS -->
    <div class="vdo-col-l">
      <div class="vdo-col-l__video">
        <iframe
          src={`https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/${videoId}?rel=0&modestbranding=1`}
          title={videoTitle}
          loading="lazy"
          allow="accelerometer; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
          allowfullscreen
        ></iframe>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="vdo-col-r">
      <h2 class="vdo-col-r__h3">Meet Joe Dampt, Vintage Guitar Expert &amp; Nationwide Buyer</h2>
      <h4 class="vdo-col-r__h4">
        <strong>12 Years &middot; 10,000+ Instruments &middot; Sellers in All 50 States</strong>
      </h4>
      <p>
        Most of the guitars I buy come with a story. A father's first electric. A guitar that toured the country in the back of a station wagon. An instrument that sat in a closet for 40 years waiting for the right home. Those stories matter to me. I document them, keep them with the instrument, and make sure they don't get lost.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm a player and a repairman who grew up on the music of Hank Garland, Merle Travis, and Chet Atkins. My own guitars are Gibson archtops, Gretsch hollowbodies, and Fender Telecasters and offsets, which is the same gear I'm buying from sellers every day. When you send me a photo of a 1950s ES-175 or a Gretsch Country Gentleman, I'm not looking it up. I already know what it is, what it's worth, and why it matters.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every guitar that comes through my shop gets a proper evaluation and any needed repairs done in-house, by me. Not by a technician I've never met. That's how I'd want my own instruments treated, and it's how I treat yours.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* vdo-sct v3 — exact rebuild of live design with video + cream bio panel */
  .vdo-sct {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 100px 24px;
    background-color: var(--color-brand-brown);
    background-image: url("/images/video-bg-01.jpg");
    background-size: cover;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-position: right center;
  }
  .vdo-sct__inner {
    position: relative;
    max-width: 1144px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 56px;
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  /* Cream backdrop behind both columns */
  .vdo-sct__inner::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    width: 101%;
    height: 120%;
    background-color: var(--color-brand-cream-warm);
    top: -10%;
    left: 0;
    z-index: -1;
  }
  /* Rust right-pointing triangle on the left edge */
  .vdo-sct__inner::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    width: 100px;
    height: 120%;
    top: -10%;
    background-color: var(--color-brand-rust-dark);
    left: 0;
    clip-path: polygon(0 0, 0 100%, 100% 50%);
    z-index: -1;
  }

  /* LEFT: video pulled left + rust border outline */
  .vdo-col-l {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .vdo-col-l::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    width: 100px;
    height: 110%;
    top: -5%;
    border: 4px solid var(--color-brand-rust-bright);
    left: -30px;
    z-index: -1;
  }
  .vdo-col-l__video {
    position: relative;
    width: 120%;
    margin-left: -15%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    z-index: 2;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }
  .vdo-col-l__video iframe {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border: 0;
  }

  /* RIGHT: cream bio panel */
  .vdo-col-r {
    background-color: var(--color-brand-cream-warm);
    padding: 30px 32px;
    color: var(--color-brand-brown);
  }
  .vdo-col-r__h3 {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-family: "Oswald", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.7vw, 30px);
    color: var(--color-brand-rust-dark);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .vdo-col-r__h4 {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    font-family: "Oswald", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 2vw, 18px);
    color: var(--color-brand-rust-dark);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  /* H4 strong has a horizontal rust accent line extending to the right */
  .vdo-col-r__h4 strong {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    padding-right: 4px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .vdo-col-r__h4 strong::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(100% + 12px);
    top: 50%;
    width: 80px;
    border-top: 3px solid var(--color-brand-rust-dark);
  }
  .vdo-col-r p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    font-family: "Open Sans", sans-serif;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-brand-brown);
  }
  .vdo-col-r p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .vdo-sct { padding: 60px 20px; }
    .vdo-sct__inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; }
    .vdo-sct__inner::after { display: none; }
    .vdo-col-l { order: 1; }
    .vdo-col-l::before { display: none; }
    .vdo-col-l__video { width: 100%; margin-left: 0; }
    .vdo-col-r { order: 2; padding: 24px; }
    .vdo-col-r__h4 strong::after { display: none; }
  }
</style>
